resumen, el equipo médico no solo se enfoca en la nutrición, sino que también abarca un enfoque integral en la atención y el tratamiento del paciente durante su proceso de recuperación.\",4\r\n6644,DRENAJE,\"DRENAJE refers to the process of removing excess fluid from the body, which can include lymphatic fluid in conditions such as chylothorax or chylous ascites, in order to alleviate symptoms. In a specific case, drainage was performed on a patient to manage the dirty output following bariatric surgery. This procedure is essential for addressing complications that may arise postoperatively, ensuring the patient's recovery and comfort.\",3\r\n11069,QUILOTÓRAX,\"QUILOTÓRAX is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of lymphatic fluid, specifically chyle, in the pleural cavity. This condition can manifest as a pleural effusion and may lead to symptoms such as dyspnea (difficulty breathing) and cough. Chylothorax can occur spontaneously or as a result of trauma, often linked to surgical procedures or disorders of the lymphatic system. Treatment for QUILOTÓRAX typically involves dietary modifications, including specific diets aimed at managing fat metabolism, as well as various medical interventions. These interventions may include surgical techniques and interventional radiology, depending on the underlying cause of the condition. Overall, careful management is essential to address the accumulation of lymphatic fluid in the pleural cavity and to alleviate associated symptoms.\",33\r\n11070,ASCITIS QUILOSA,\"Ascitis quilosa is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of chyle, a lymphatic fluid, in the abdominal cavity. This condition often arises due to the rupture or obstruction of abdominal lymphatic ducts and is typically observed around the fifth postoperative day when patients have begun an oral diet. Ascitis quilosa can lead to significant nutritional deficiencies and may necessitate dietary modifications or surgical intervention. It is associated with various medical conditions and can cause symptoms such as abdominal distension. Treatment approaches for ascitis quilosa may include conservative management or surgical options, depending on the severity and underlying causes. In summary, ascitis quilosa involves the accumulation of lymphatic fluid in the peritoneal cavity, requiring specific medical and dietary management to address the associated complications.\",27\r\n3692,SOMATOSTATINA,\"SOMATOSTATINA is a hormone produced by pancreatic delta cells that plays a crucial role in inhibiting the secretion of several other hormones, including growth hormone (GH), thyrotropin-releasing hormone (TRH), prolactin (PRL), and adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH) in the pituitary gland. This inhibitory function makes somatostatin significant in various medical treatments. \n\nSomatostatin is utilized in the treatment of pituitary tumors and is effective in managing complications following surgery, such as anastomotic dehiscence. Additionally, it is employed in the treatment of specific conditions like chylothorax and lymphatic fistulas, where it helps reduce gastrointestinal secretions and lymphatic flow. \n\nMoreover, somatostatin analogs are medications derived from this hormone that can be administered in parenteral nutrition under specific circumstances. These analogs are particularly useful in treating VIPoma, a type of tumor that secretes vasoactive intestinal peptide, by inhibiting its secretion. They are also used in managing acromegaly, a condition characterized by excessive growth hormone, and are often combined with dietary modifications to enhance treatment efficacy.\",9\r\n114,NEOPLASIAS,\"NEOPLASIAS refer to abnormal growths of tissue that can manifest in various forms and lead to a range of medical complications. These growths can cause significant issues such as intestinal obstruction and malnutrition, often necessitating nutritional support through parenteral nutrition. Additionally, neoplasias can result in conditions like ascitis quilosa and quilotórax, which are associated with fluid accumulation in the body. Tumors located in the throat or esophagus can obstruct swallowing, leading to dysphagia, and may require interventions such as gastrostomy for nutritional support. Furthermore, dietary factors can influence the development of neoplasms, which are recognized as a significant cause of mortality worldwide. Overall, neoplasias represent a serious health concern due to their potential to disrupt normal bodily functions and contribute to severe health complications.\",4\r\n11102,TRATAMIENTO FARMACOLÓGICO,\"The entity \"\"TRATAMIENTO FARMACOLÓGICO\"\" refers to pharmacological treatment, which involves the use of medications to manage various medical conditions. Specifically, it includes the administration of drugs such as somatostatin or octreotide, which are utilized to address conditions like quilotórax (chylothorax) and ascitis quilosa (chylous ascites). Additionally, pharmacological treatment may also affect a patient's ability to receive enteral nutrition, indicating that the use of these medications can have implications for nutritional management in patients undergoing such treatments.\",2\r\n11158,TRATAMIENTO QUIRÚRGICO,\"The entity \"\"TRATAMIENTO QUIRÚRGICO\"\" refers to surgical treatment options indicated for various medical conditions. Specifically, surgical treatment is recommended for patients suffering from severe pancreatic conditions, especially in cases where complications arise, such as bile duct obstruction or the presence of pseudo cysts. Additionally, surgical intervention is advised for refractory cases of chylothorax and chylous ascites, which involves procedures aimed at repairing injuries to the lymphatic ducts. This comprehensive approach highlights the critical role of surgical treatment in managing complex medical issues.\",4\r\n11025,INMUNOGLOBULINAS,\"Immunoglobulins, also known as \"\"inmunoglobulinas,\"\" are antibodies produced by the immune system that play a crucial role in identifying and neutralizing pathogens such as bacteria and viruses. They are essential components of the immune response and are found in bodily fluids like chyle. In addition to their protective functions, inmunoglobulinas have been investigated as immunosuppressive agents in the treatment of autoimmune liver disease (ALD) to help reduce inflammation. However, studies have indicated that they have not demonstrated significant clinical improvement in this context. Overall, inmunoglobulinas are vital for immune defense while also being explored for their potential therapeutic applications in certain medical conditions.\",3\r\n10513,LINFOMA,\"Lymphoma is a type of cancer that primarily affects the lymphatic system, which is a crucial part of the immune system. This condition can lead to various complications, including ascitis quilosa, a specific type of fluid accumulation in the abdominal cavity. Additionally, lymphoma may be associated with refractory celiac disease, and it can present with gastrointestinal symptoms, highlighting its potential impact on digestive health.\",2\r\n11085,SISTEMA LINFÁTICO,\"The \"\"SISTEMA LINFÁTICO\"\" is a vital system in the body responsible for transporting lymph, a fluid that contains white blood cells and various other components, through lymphatic vessels to the circulatory system. It is a complex network of tissues and organs that plays a crucial role in the body's immune function by helping to eliminate toxins, waste, and other unwanted materials. This system is essential for maintaining overall health and supporting the body's defense mechanisms.\",8\r\n11156,OCTREOTIDA,\"Octreotide is a synthetic analog of somatostatin, primarily utilized in the treatment of various medical conditions, including quilotórax and ascitis quilosa. It is often administered through continuous infusion. In addition to its standalone use, octreotide is also employed in conjunction with dietary treatments to help reduce lymphatic flow, thereby enhancing clinical outcomes for patients.\",4\r\n11084,CONDUCTO TORÁCICO,\"El conducto torácico es un conducto linfático que transporta la linfa desde el sistema linfático al sistema venoso, desembocando en la confluencia de la vena subclavia y la vena yugular interna izquierdas.\",3\r\n11157,ETILNEFRINA,Etilnefrina is a sympathomimetic drug that reduces lymphatic flow in the thoracic duct by contracting the smooth muscle of its wall.,2\r\n2834,FIBRINÓGENO,\"Fibrinogen is a crucial blood plasma protein that plays a vital role in blood clot formation and wound healing. It is essential for the coagulation process, helping to prevent excessive bleeding when injuries occur. Additionally, fibrinogen levels are closely monitored in patients undergoing anticoagulation therapy and those with thrombotic conditions, as these levels can indicate the body's ability to form clots effectively. Overall, fibrinogen is integral to maintaining hemostasis and is a key factor in the management of various blood-related health issues.\",2\r\n11162,FÍSTULAS QUILOSAS,,2\r\n11099,LINFOCITOS T,\"LINFOCITOS T, or T lymphocytes, are a type of white blood cell that play a central role in cell-mediated immunity. They are crucial for the immune response, helping the body to identify and eliminate pathogens and infected cells.\",2\r\n11103,TRATAMIENTO CONSERVADOR,\"\"\"TRATAMIENTO CONSERVADOR\"\" refers to a management approach that employs non-surgical methods to address medical conditions such as chylothorax and chylous ascites. This treatment strategy emphasizes dietary modifications and medical therapies as initial interventions, prioritizing resolution of the condition without resorting to invasive surgical options.\",2\r\n11161,EMBOLIZACIÓN,\"Embolization is a minimally invasive procedure used to treat conditions such as quilotórax and lymphatic fistulas, showing high success rates in traumatic cases.\",1\r\n11100,LINFOCITOS B,B lymphocytes are a type of white blood cell that produce antibodies and are essential for humoral immunity.,1\r\n11097,LINFOGRAFÍA,La linfografía es una técnica de imagen utilizada para evaluar el sistema linfático y puede ser útil en el diagnóstico de quilotórax.,1\r\n11093,TORACOCENTESIS,\"La toracocentesis es un procedimiento médico utilizado para extraer líquido del espacio pleural, que puede ayudar en el diagnóstico del quilotórax.\",1\r\n11096,TÉCNICAS DE IMAGEN,Las técnicas de imagen son métodos utilizados para diagnosticar y localizar lesiones en condiciones como el quilotórax.,1\r\n11101,QUILOTÓRAX ASOCIADO A TUMOR,\"Quilotórax associated with a tumor refers to the condition of lymphatic fluid accumulation in the pleural cavity that is linked to the presence of a tumor, affecting prognosis.\",1\r\n4388,TOMOGRAFÍA AXIAL COMPUTARIZADA,\"Tomografía Axial Computarizada, also known as CT scan, is a diagnostic imaging technique utilized to create detailed images of internal organs, which is frequently employed in medical evaluations. This advanced imaging method allows for the identification of the location and causes of various medical conditions, including specific issues such as chylothorax.\",1\r\n10173,TIPS,\"TIPS, or Transjugular Intrahepatic Portosystemic Shunt, is a medical procedure designed to address portal hypertension, which is frequently associated with liver disease. This procedure is particularly beneficial for treating conditions such as quilotórax that arise as a secondary complication of portal hypertension. By creating a shunt, TIPS offers a potential resolution for these conditions, improving patient outcomes related to elevated portal pressure.\",1\r\n11088,AMILOIDOSIS,\"Amyloidosis is a disease characterized by the accumulation of amyloid proteins in various organs, which can lead to serious health conditions. This condition can result in complications such as ascitis quilosa and is associated with chronic intestinal pseudo-obstruction, affecting multiple organs, including the gastrointestinal system. The buildup of these abnormal proteins can impair the function of the intestines, potentially affecting nutrient absorption and necessitating the use of parenteral nutrition for affected individuals.\",1\r\n11086,CARCINOMATOSIS PERITONEAL,\"Peritoneal carcinomatosis refers to the spread of cancer to the peritoneum, which can cause ascitis quilosa.\",1\r\n11092,QUILOTÓRAX CONGÉNITO,,1\r\n11087,SARCOMA DE KAPOSI,Kaposi's sarcoma is a type of cancer that can lead to complications such as ascitis quilosa.,1\r\n11089,LINFANGIOLEIOMATOSIS,Lymphangioleiomyomatosis is a rare lung disease that can cause chylothorax and may be associated with ascitic conditions.,1\r\n11090,TROMBOSIS VENA SUBCLAVIA IZQUIERDA,\"Left subclavian vein thrombosis can lead to complications affecting lymphatic drainage, potentially resulting in ascitis quilosa.\",1\r\n11091,BOCIO ENDOTORÁCICO,\"Endothoracic goiter is a condition that can cause obstruction of lymphatic flow, potentially leading to ascitic conditions.\",1\r\n11094,PARACENTESIS,\"La paracentesis es un procedimiento médico para extraer líquido del abdomen, utilizado en el diagnóstico de ascitis quilosa.\",1\r\n11160,FLUJO LINFÁTICO,,3\r\n3267,LINFOCITOS,\"Linfocitos, or lymphocytes, are a type of white blood cell that play a crucial role in the immune system. They are found in the chyle and are essential for immune function. The count of lymphocytes is an important parameter used in diagnosing malnutrition and assessing nutritional health. Specifically, lymphocyte levels are included in the Nutritional Index of Pinato, which helps evaluate an individual's nutritional status. Overall, lymphocytes serve as indicators of both immune function and nutritional well-being.\",2\r\n11159,FÍSTULAS LINFÁTICAS,\"Lymphatic fistulas are abnormal connections that can form between lymphatic vessels and other structures, often requiring surgical intervention.\",1\r\n13783,ALOANTÍGENOS,\"Los aloantígen